  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Sagittine G and the CD276 antigen through a series of target interactions. Sagittine G is predicted to target DNA polymerase iota, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-((4-(Ethylamino)-6-methoxy-1,3,5-triazin-2-yl)amino)-2-methylpropiononitrile and (6S,10S)-6,10,14-trimethylpentadecan-2-one. These compounds are also predicted to target the CD276 antigen, indicating a possible pathway through which Sagittine G may influence the CD276 antigen. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential role of Sagittine G in modulating the CD276 antigen through the regulation of DNA polymerase iota, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm this interaction.",
